          "text": "Division of Social Services"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Economic Independence Section • 325 North Salisbury Street\n2420 Mail Service Center • Raleigh, North Carolina 27699-2420\nCourier # 56-20-25"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Michael F. Easley, Governor\nCarmen Hooker Buell, Secretary"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Pheon E. Beal, Director\n(919) 733-3055"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "May 17, 2002"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "**Re:\tWORK FIRST APPLICANT SURVEY\n\tJune 2002**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "**Dear County Director of Social Services:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "**Attention: Work First Supervisors and Program Administrators**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "During the months of November and December 2001 county DSS Work First staff completed a **Work First Applicant Survey** for Work First or Benefit Diversion applicants. An analysis of the information collected during that time period has been shared with counties and with the Economic Services Committee and Employment Programs Committee of the North Carolina Association of County Directors of Social Services."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "During that time period, and for several months prior, the state realized a net monthly increase in the overall Work First caseload. At the time, we were very concerned that the overall caseload increase, which endured for six months, would continue. Fortunately, beginning in February 2002, the overall caseload has slightly decreased each subsequent month (through first of the month caseload data for May 2002)."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The information you provided was most valuable as we planned for potential impact on resources and service delivery. With clear information regarding applicant characteristics and causal factors, county DSS staff as well as Division staff were better equipped to respond to an increase in requests for information about new applicants from a variety of sources, including social services boards, boards of county commissioners, the media, etc."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "At its February 2002 meeting, the Employment Programs Committee voted to request that the survey be repeated in June 2002 and November 2002. Information from surveys at these points of time will provide additional information regarding any significant change in applicant demographics and causal factors for applying for assistance."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Through the use of the attached data collection tool, which can be keyed electronically or manually checked, we are again requesting your assistance in collecting characteristic and causal factor information on individuals for whom your staff completes applications for Work First or Benefit Diversion during June 2002. The survey form provides us with information currently unavailable through our automated systems."
        },
        {
          "type": "header_footer",
          "subtype": "footer",
          "text": "An Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer"
        }
      ],
